Built `compress.py` as a stdlib-only structured compressor that stores header fields compactly and converts hexadecimal and base-36 records to binary, with a matching decompressor. Verified byte-identical round-tripping of `corpus_hard.txt`; the archive is 18,232 bytes versus 44,267 bytes input (58.8136% reduction), beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. The registered round-trip assay passed consistently.